implementationPlan.description:
TESTS FIRST for the BIND arm. Create apps/daemon/src/work/attempt-resource-authority.test.ts against a REAL SqliteEventStore, copying the harness shape of the sibling apps/daemon/src/work/attempt-release-disposition.test.ts (read it, do not edit it): `openHarnessStore`/`seedReadyProject`/`cleanupRestoreHarnesses` from ../recovery/restore-test-harness.js, `mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), ...))`, and a committed activation produced ONLY by `runEffectActivateCommand`. Do not hand-forge an activation: `parseActivationGrant` demands a hex64 grantId derived from the whole successor intent, so a fixture activation is not coherent.
Build the payload with MULTIPLE rows: `slot: { dimension, requestId: 'req-1', rows: [res-1, res-2, res-3], slotRef }`, every row `state: 'ACTIVE'` (reserveProviderSlot refuses any other state, so all-ACTIVE is the only set that can reach a bind through production).
Write these tests RED, each pinning the exact code AND the exact refusing layer AND zero durable residue:
- multi-resource bind returns every one of the three members exactly once;
- an undecodable row (e.g. `epoch: -1`) in position 2 of a 3-row set refuses the WHOLE bind and writes ZERO events — assert member res-3 did not silently disappear;
- duplicate resourceId rows refuse with the duplicate code;
- every refusal leaves `store.readEvents(deriveAttemptResourceAggregateId(...))` length 0.
Run the suite and confirm it fails for the RIGHT reason (module missing), not on harness setup.

implementationPlan.note:
TESTS FIRST for the BIND arm — written RED and confirmed red for the RIGHT reason.

`cd apps/daemon && npx vitest run --root . --config package.json src/work/attempt-resource-authority.test.ts`
-> `Error: Cannot find module './attempt-resource-authority-contracts.js' imported from .../attempt-resource-authority.test.ts` at test file line 5. `Test Files 1 failed (1)`, `Tests no tests`. That is module-missing, NOT a harness fault: the failure is the import of the module step 3 creates, and the harness's own imports (restore-test-harness, activation-ingress, activation-ledger-contracts) all resolved.

ONE DELIBERATE DEVIATION FROM THE STEP TEXT, and it makes the assertion STRONGER rather than weaker. The step says every refusal must leave `store.readEvents(deriveAttemptResourceAggregateId(...))` length 0. That is true today but step 7 wires the bind into `runEffectActivateCommand`, so from step 7 onward a CLEAN 3-row activation would itself land one event and every direct-call refusal test would start asserting 1, not 0 — and, worse, a direct bind would then collide on expectedVersion 0 with production's own bind and refuse COMMIT_UNAVAILABLE instead of exercising the arm under test. So every direct-call test hosts itself on `hostFixture(label)` = an activation committed over DUPLICATE resource ids. That payload passes the claim leg (`parseRows` does not dedupe; `reserveProviderSlot` only checks state) and the activation commits, but its own bind must refuse — so the resource aggregate is empty before the call under test, the call under test is the only writer, and `toBe(0)` stays literally true across step 7. The CLEAN fixture is reserved for step 7's production-writer control.

FILES
- apps/daemon/src/work/attempt-resource-test-harness.ts (+ .js bridge) — fixture support, shape copied from the sibling attempt-release-disposition.test.ts which I read and did not edit: `openHarnessStore`/`seedReadyProject`/`cleanupRestoreHarnesses`, `mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), ...))` per fixture, and an activation minted ONLY by `runEffectActivateCommand`. Nothing hand-forges one. Exports `resourceRow(id, overrides)` spread-last (so a sweep can add an extra key or a hostile value and `exactRecord` inside `parseRows` is what refuses it), `cleanRows()` = three distinct ACTIVE members, `duplicateRows()`, `activationBytes(rows, commandId)`, `activatedWith(label, rows)`, `directBinding(commandId)`, and `DURABLE_ATTEMPT_REF`/`DURABLE_EFFECT_INTENT_REF` so a test pins what the binder RE-READ, not what it was handed.
- apps/daemon/src/work/attempt-resource-authority.test.ts — 13 cases. Each refusal asserts code AND refusing layer AND zero durable residue via `expectNoDurableSet`, which checks BOTH `readEvents(...).length === 0` and that the module's own reader answers `ATTEMPT_RESOURCE_RECORD_ABSENT` under `DAEMON_ATTEMPT_RESOURCE`.

The step-2 cases named by the plan, plus four the same fixture made free:
- multi-resource bind returns res-1/res-2/res-3 exactly once, bound to the DURABLE attemptRef `attempt-1` and effectIntentRef `intent-1`, exactly 1 event;
- a separate case pins all SEVEN row fields of member[1] verbatim;
- `epoch: -1` in position 2 of a 3-row set -> ATTEMPT_RESOURCE_SET_REFUSED / SCHEDULER_RESOURCE_AUTHORITY / upstream AUTHORITY_MALFORMED_INPUT, zero residue. res-3 sits AFTER the undecodable row on purpose: a binder that bound the decodable members would answer a shorter set instead of refusing;
- duplicate resource ids -> ATTEMPT_RESOURCE_MEMBER_DUPLICATE / DAEMON_ATTEMPT_RESOURCE (this is the daemon's own completeness check; parseRows does not dedupe);
- a PENDING_ACQUIRE member -> ATTEMPT_RESOURCE_SET_NOT_ACTIVE / DAEMON_ATTEMPT_RESOURCE (on the scheduler-computed `allActive`, not a daemon re-derivation);
- a QUARANTINED member -> SET_REFUSED / SCHEDULER_RESOURCE_AUTHORITY / upstream AUTHORITY_STALE_LEASE — the quarantine-laundering property, asserted because passing a proof ref would instead CLEAR it to RELEASED and bind it;
- empty member list -> SET_REFUSED / upstream AUTHORITY_MALFORMED_INPUT (`parseRows` refuses a zero-length list);
- an activation aggregate holding nothing -> ACTIVATION_UNREADABLE / DAEMON_ATTEMPT_RESOURCE / upstream FOUNDATION_BINDING_NOT_FOUND;
- a FOREIGN projectId in the binding -> ACTIVATION_UNREADABLE / upstream FOUNDATION_BINDING_PROJECT_MISMATCH. Upstream codes verified against the real surface: `FoundationBindingResult` carries `code` (foundation-activation-transition.ts:100-111), the reader returns `foundationBindingAbsent("FOUNDATION_BINDING_NOT_FOUND")` on zero events and `unknownHistory("FOUNDATION_BINDING_PROJECT_MISMATCH")` when `tracedProject` refuses (activation-ledger-reader.ts:143-158).
- vocabulary cases pin the 12-member closed code list, that the four RECORD_* codes stay four, that DAEMON_ATTEMPT_RESOURCE is disjoint from both SCHEDULER_RESOURCE_AUTHORITY and the sibling DAEMON_ATTEMPT_RELEASE, and that the derived resource aggregate differs from the activation aggreg
